# Rust
target/
engine/target/

# Coverage
.coverage/

# What shellops generates and nothing tracks: the tooling cache `ops install`
# provisions and the compiled trees beside it (.ops/cache, carried between CI
# jobs), the test-selection metrics records, the trace maps and the
# full-suite junit reports (CI keeps them as artifacts, outside the cache),
# and the compiled tree, the link into the cache .envrc derives from the
# sources, and the reference `ops docs` renders from it, which the trunk's
# pipeline keeps as an artifact (ADR 000047). Anchored to the project root, because in a consuming
# repo `.ops` is also the submodule mount point.
/.ops/cache/
/.ops/testing-metrics/
/.ops/testing-trace/
/.ops/__compiled__*
/.ops/docs/

# What terraform init writes beside .ops/infra: the provider binaries and the
# backend configuration, which carries the state address of the last run.
/.ops/infra/.terraform/

# Toolchain homes. The CI presets point CARGO_HOME and RUSTUP_HOME here and
# cache them between jobs, so a job that provisions rust leaves them untracked.
/.cargo/
/.rustup/
__pycache__/
